package UI

// A view is a UI<M>: an immutable tree whose buttons and inputs send values
// of the app's message enum M (README "Typed views"). Bare UI in a function's
// signature takes the message type of its arguments.
//
// UI.Button(label, on, enabled), and the inputs in UI.Inputs.oct, are
// compiler-owned: they are generic over the message enum, which an ordinary
// Oct function cannot be. They are reached through the UI namespace and can
// be written as markup tags (<UI.Button Label="Save" On={Msg.Save} Enabled={true} />).

// The canonical text form of a view: node kinds, ids, specs and messages.
// Tests compare views by it.
fn Signature(node: UI) -> String {
    return UISignature(node)
}
